{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["And the reason for <b>unto His dwelling shall you seek</b>: that you shall go to Him from distant lands and ask, \"Where is the road to the house of HaShem?\" and say, each man to his fellow, \"Come, let us go up to the mountain of YHWH, to the house of the Elohim of Jacob\" (Isaiah 2:3), in the manner of \"They shall ask for Zion, that is the way; their faces are toward it\" (Jeremiah 50:5). And in the Sifrei (Re'eh 8): \"'You shall seek' — seek by the mouth of a prophet.\" One might think you wait until a prophet tells you — Scripture says, \"unto His dwelling shall you seek, and you shall come there\" — seek and find, and afterward a prophet will tell you. And so you find in the case of David, etc. And by way of truth, \"unto His dwelling shall you seek\" — for His glory shall you seek. \"And you shall come there\" — to see the face of the Master, YHWH, the Elohim of Israel. And from this the Sages derived the term \"Shekhinah.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The citation from the Sifrei paraphrases a beraita found in Sifrei Devarim 62; the exact chapter numbering varies between editions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:48:33.442964229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}